<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper Burgundy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">888–933</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Kingdom of Upper Burgundy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> was a kingdom founded in 888 by the Welf Rudolf I, crowned at Saint-Maurice d'Agaune, covering the lands between the Jura and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennine-alps">Pennine Alps</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-geneva">Lake Geneva</a> and the later Franche-Comté. Around 933 his son Rudolf II united it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burgundy">Lower Burgundy</a>, the kingdom of Provence, to form the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a>, which passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> in 1032.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/upper-burgundy.jpg" alt="Upper Burgundy" width="320" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (Sidonius) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Hoch_und_Niederburgund_EN.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
